d he says  that within a few years this is I guess  as the war is about ending within a few  years Hitler will emerge from the hatred  that surrounds him now as one of the  most significant figures who ever lived  what do you think Jack Kennedy meant by  that well there's actually an additional  sentence  beyond that one that you just relic  about quoting that of context where he  does mention that you know certainly he  was nothing short of wholly evil but he  will be one of remembered as one of the  most significant figures in history and  I can only assume that that's what he  meant by it um certainly the children's  letters although Joe Kennedy after 1938  in particular peppers a number of his  diary entries and correspondences with  an anti-semitic remarks and that was  never the case among his children's  letters that I've that I found with one  exception in young Joe's letters but it  was never the case for Jack so I can  only assume given the totality of his  other writings that that's what he meant  that Hitler will be recalled as a very  significant although evil figure you say  in the book that you have one vivid  personal memory of Joe Kennedy when you  went to the house the summer before he  died  summer of 69 what was that memory well I  remember I was about 2 at the time and I  remember being holding the babysitter's  hand and walking across the lawn at the  Cape and my cousin who was about the  same age at the time was there too and  we were both trundling across the lawn  and we were told that we were going to  see grandpa and I remember also hearing  from the conversation that was going on  between the two babysitter's that we  were also going to see mr. Kennedy and  the ambassador and I got very suspicious  that we're gonna actually have to walk a  lot further than I'd originally imagined  so I wasn't looking forward to it and  then I remember being told that we had  to curtsy I had to curtsy because I was  a little girl and my cousin being a boy 