ion  or with his unpopularity in England and  all of that is certainly well documented  and absolutely true and many  BECs but on the other hand what struck  me about his correspondence was how much  more nuance that created from him and  let's say the broad brushstrokes are  there and well established but he's a  much more subtle figure in my mind than  he ever was before and although he was  somebody who was in a very slow to  forgive anybody crossing him he was also  somebody who had enormous sort of tender  affection and that's something that I  didn't quite expect how what a soft side  he had I've recited that litany of names  that he has had to carry through his  life and after his death the philanderer  anti-semite bootlegger as well as film  producer financier banker kingmaker  other any of those that you would leave  out in retrospect that you would not  apply to Joe Kennedy in retrospect I'd  say again that you know there's there's  something to many of those but I would  say that there's a certain nuance that I  think his own papers and many papers  that are available about him bring to it  and in terms of bootlegging for example  although it's often been said that he  had sort of an enormous and well  organized operation bringing alcohol  into the North Shore of Boston during  the 20s there's no particular indication  that that was true but there is actual  very concrete documentation among his  own papers that um when Prohibition came  into effect in 1920 his father who among  other things was the owner of some  saloons stored their alcohol and one of  the things about prohibition that I'm  sure many of you know is that it didn't  actually make the possession of alcohol  illegal it just made selling it illegal  so the family kept all these stores of  alcohol for their own consumption but  also Joe Kennedy supplied 190 proof  alcohol to his tenth reunion at Harvard  in 1922 and I was reading over the  belief --let's from that were generated  over the cou